/-!
# The generation condition of a quadruple over an affine base

Let `S` be a scheme, `𝒜` a graded `𝒪_S`-algebra all of whose homogeneous pieces are
quasi-coherent (Situation 01NN), fix `d`, and let `(d, f : T → S, L, ψ)` be a quadruple over a
test scheme `T` (Section 01NS). Part of the data of a quadruple is that the degree-one component
`ψ_1 : f^*𝒜_d ⟶ L` be *surjective*; part of the data of a triple (Section 01N4) is instead that
`L` be *generated by the global sections* `ψ(a)`, `a ∈ A_d = Γ(S, 𝒜_d)`. For `S` affine the
second follows from the first, and that is what this module proves.

The sections in question are
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf.Twisting.degreeOneSectionHom`, and the
conclusion is stated in the geometric form Section 27.12 uses the generation condition: the
nonvanishing opens of those sections cover `T`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf.epi_freeHomEquiv_symm_id`: **a quasi-coherent
  module on an affine scheme is generated by the family of all of its global sections**, the
  index type being the module of global sections itself.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf.epi_pullbackGenHom`: the pullback of that
  family along any morphism of schemes still generates, the generators being the pullback-unit
  images of the global sections.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf.Quadruple.iSup_nonvanishingOpen_eq_top`:
  **the generation condition.** For `S` affine, the nonvanishing opens of the global sections
  `ψ(a)` of `L`, `a ∈ Γ(S, 𝒜_d)`, cover `T`.

## The route

The surjectivity of `ψ_1` is an epimorphism of sheaves of modules, so it may simply be composed
with a generating family of `f^*𝒜_d`, and such a family is produced from one on the base:

* over an affine scheme a quasi-coherent module `N` is generated by its global sections, so the
  morphism `𝒪_S^{(Γ(S,N))} ⟶ N` reading off the global sections is an epimorphism. The index
  type is all of `Γ(S, N)` rather than a chosen generating set, which is what lets the
  conclusion be indexed by `Γ(S, 𝒜_d)`;
* `f^*` is a left adjoint, so it preserves epimorphisms, and it carries a free module to the
  free module on the same index type, `f^*(𝒪_S^{(I)}) ≅ 𝒪_T^{(I)}`. Composing gives an
  epimorphism `𝒪_T^{(Γ(S,N))} ⟶ f^*N`, and the global section it attaches to `a ∈ Γ(S, N)` is
  the pullback-unit image of `a`, which is what the transposed map of
  `...RelativeProjQcohSheaf.Twisting.sectionHom` is built from;
* composing with `ψ_1` and with the identification `L^{⊗ 1} ≅ L` of Tag 01CU gives a generating
  family of global sections of `L` whose member at `a` is `ψ(a)`, and a generating family of
  global sections of an *invertible* module has at every point a member that does not vanish
  there (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_generatingSection_nonvanishing`), because the germs span
  the stalk while the maximal ideal does not kill it.

Two transports are bookkeeping: the degree-one component of `ψ` is indexed by `𝒜_{1 · d}` while
the sections of a triple are indexed by `𝒜_d`, and the pullback-unit image of a section over `S`
lives over `f⁻¹S` rather than over `T`. Both are already carried by
`Twisting.globalSectionHom` and `Twisting.degreeOneSectionHom`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NU)
* [Stacks Project, Section 01N4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N4)
* [Stacks Project, Section 01NS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NS)
